From 1eb2d20d4a0620d9208015a6c538730436a0a0f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:30:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/51] Add the Baidu and Niutrans translation engines

Two more traditional machine translation providers join the engine
list, following their public API documentation:

- Baidu general translation API: credentials go into the API key
  field as "appid#secret" (hinted in the settings), every request
  is signed with MD5(appid + q + salt + secret), and the request
  text is split to stay below the 6000-byte q limit. The standard
  tier allows one request per second, so chunks pause 1050 ms in
  between, rate-limit replies (54003) are retried with a pause, and
  the engine's default concurrency is one.
- Niutrans text translation API: newline-joined requests with the
  line structure preserved in tgt_text, line-by-line fallback when
  a reply does not match up, and a default concurrency of two for
  the free tier's rate limit.

Each engine now also carries its own recommended defaults: profiles
without stored tuning fall back to the provider's values instead of
the generic ones, and switching the provider resets the concurrency
and batch size accordingly (users can still raise them for paid
tiers). Baidu's language codes (jp, kor, fra, spa, rus, vie, ara,
cht) are mapped in engineTargetCode, and both engines show their
display names in the profile picker and settings summaries.
